{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"extralegal-romantic-tuna","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py` requires a plan-review attestation for a bug fix over 150 non-test lines. When the attestation classification itself raises (`classify_plan_review_attestation` catches every exception and returns `verdict: \"error\"`), `apply_bugfix_size_gate` maps INFRA to an **advisory** finding (module docstring: \"INFRA → advisory finding\") and the change keeps `LLM-Review +1`. An infrastructure fault therefore produces the same outcome as a satisfied gate.\n\n## Reproduction\n- Gerrit change 1369 (`73abb5805f`, trailer ticket e39f, type bug, 525 non-test lines) merged on `LLM-Review +1` with 0 blocking / 2 advisory findings; the REVIEW_RESULT coverage records the bugfix-size gate as `error`. The ticket `asbestos-lithe-kouprey` (b6e1-c217-8cd3-4446) was later filed against that change.\n- Unit: make `_load_ticket_state` raise inside `classify_plan_review_attestation`; `apply_bugfix_size_gate` leaves `verdict` unchanged from PASS.\n\n## Expected\nAn infrastructure error in a blocking gate abstains instead of passing: the verdict becomes INDETERMINATE (no `LLM-Review` vote cast, matching the review-bot abstain posture in story `contrived-enslaved-cow` S4 \"no false content vote on infra failure\"), with the classification error surfaced in the coverage record so the bot's infra-recovery loop (story `subtle-sludgy-earthworm` S5) re-runs it.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a RED test: classification error on a >150-line bug-fix diff yields `verdict == \"INDETERMINATE\"` and a coverage entry `bugfix_size_gate.verdict == \"error\"`, no advisory finding that reads as a pass.\n- Change the INFRA arm of `apply_bugfix_size_gate` to set INDETERMINATE; leave `unsigned`/`stale-material` (BLOCK) and satisfied (no-op) arms unchanged.\n- Keep the ≤150-line no-op and the missing-trailer no-op unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A classification error on an over-floor bug fix produces an INDETERMINATE review verdict, not PASS; checked by the new unit test in `tests/unit/llm/code_review/`.\n- [ ] Existing tests for `unsigned`, `stale-material`, certified, and under-floor behaviour pass unchanged; checked by `pytest tests/unit -k bugfix_size`.\n- [ ] The Gerrit voter casts no `LLM-Review` vote for INDETERMINATE (existing behaviour), confirmed by the voter's unit test; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -k indeterminate`.\n\n## Verification\n`pytest tests/unit -k \"bugfix_size or review_bot\"`; `make lint`; `make typecheck`.","id":"9011-54d6-eb04-4cd6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["gates","code-review","fail-open","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"bugfix-size attestation gate degrades to advisory on classification error, so an infra fault passes the change"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787354597536923001,"uuid":"795f9d50-6134-4514-a6ef-a5891be34e97"}